course: dictionary
lesson: 8929
title: Signals all around us
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A signal is a sound, light, sign or movement that gives a message or warning. A red traffic light is a signal: it tells drivers to stop. You can often understand a signal without a single word.
explain: «Cyclists use hand signals to show when they turn.» The rider's arm is sending a message to the drivers behind. To check your meaning, swap in the word message: «Cyclists use hand messages to show when they turn» is odd, so signal here means a movement that gives a message.
explain: Signal can also be a verb. «She signalled for the bus to stop» means she gave the driver a message by waving or raising her hand. Signals can also be radio waves that carry sound, pictures and data to phones, TVs and radios.
fact: A signal is a sound, light, sign or movement that gives a message or warning.
fact: Signal can be a noun (a signal) or a verb (to signal).
fact: «Signal» can mean radio waves that carry sound, pictures or data to phones, TVs and radios.
fact: «No signal» means the phone cannot connect.
fact: «Signal» as a verb means to give a message by a movement, light or sound, such as «signal for help».
exercise: «The driver saw the red traffic signal and stopped.» What is a traffic signal? | A sound | A type of car | A kind of road | *A light or sign that tells drivers to stop or go
exercise: «Ravi signalled to his friend across the playground.» What does signalled mean? | Fell asleep | Shouted every word | Ran away | *Gave a message with a wave or sign
exercise: Mum says, «There's no signal.» What does she mean? | The phone is too big to hold | *The phone cannot connect | The screen is too bright | The phone is fully charged
test: «If a rip current carries you, float and signal for help.» What is a good way to signal for help? | Dive under the water | Swim straight back against the current | *Wave a torch or blow a whistle | Shout nothing and wait
test: Which of these is a signal? | *A hand held out to show a turn | A pencil case | A bag of sweets | A pair of shoes
exam: A rail worker waves a red flag at the train. What is the flag doing? | Measuring the speed of the train | Decorating the train | *Giving a message or warning, which makes it a signal | Cleaning the track
